  "goodToKnow": "Der Pendler (die Pendlerin) is a commuter. Around 20 million Germans commute to another municipality for work, and Munich and Frankfurt attract the most. Pendeln means to commute, like a pendulum (das Pendel) swinging back and forth. Commuters can claim the Pendlerpauschale (commuter allowance) in their tax return, a long-debated subsidy. Plural: die Pendler."
